      "text": "What's in application context?"
    },
    {
      "scene": 2,
      "start": 1.955542,
      "end": 7.248583,
      "text": "Bean definitions are recipes. Managed instances are the actual objects."
    },
    {
      "scene": 3,
      "start": 7.428583,
      "end": 14.66925,
      "text": "Register configuration, then refresh. Spring reads the definitions and creates our singleton beans."
    },
    {
      "scene": 4,
      "start": 14.84925,
      "end": 19.733417,
      "text": "Calling get bean returns the service, already wired to its repository."
    },
    {
      "scene": 5,
      "start": 19.913417,
      "end": 24.828792,
      "text": "The context also publishes events. Close it, and managed cleanup runs."
    },
    {
      "scene": 6,
      "start": 25.008792,
      "end": 32.1485,
      "text": "Our tests confirm: same service, one event, cleanup called. Definitions describe; instances do the work."
